==Trivia==
*Her Japanese name, Namie-chan, may be a reference to [[wikipedia:Namie Amuro|Namie Amuro]], also known as Amuro-chan.
**Since both are famous singers, songwriters, actresses and producers, this could mean that her English name is, by extension, a reference to [[wikipedia:Selena Gomez|Selena Gomez]].
*Her design is likely meant to resemble the [[wikipedia:Ganguro|Ganguro]] subculture's style of make-up and accessories.

